            <h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
            <h3>How Often Should a Washing Machine Be Cleaned?</h3>
            <p>
              A thorough cleaning should be carried out approximately once a month, especially when the washing machine is used frequently or mainly operates at low temperatures. The detergent drawer and rubber door seal should be inspected and cleaned more frequently whenever visible residue, moisture or an unpleasant smell is present.
            </p>
            <h3>Can Washing Machine Cleaner Damage Coloured Laundry During the Next Cycle?</h3>
            <p>
              This should not happen when the product is used correctly and the instructions on the packaging are followed. After the cleaning programme has finished, check that no product residue remains inside the drum or detergent drawer. When in doubt, run an additional rinse cycle before adding coloured clothes.
            </p>
            <h3>How Do You Clean a Washer-Dryer Without Damaging the Drying System?</h3>
            <p>
              Use only cleaning methods and products that are suitable for a combined washer-dryer. Do not add unmeasured amounts of vinegar, baking soda or citric acid, as these substances may damage the seals and other components. Clean the accessible filters and surfaces according to the appliance manual, and use the maintenance programme if your model is equipped with one.
            </p>

            <p class="disclaimer">
              This article has been prepared for informational purposes and does not replace professional technical diagnostics.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
